details:
(a) the progress of PM Surya Ghar: Muft Bijli Yojana in Nagaland, the number of households in Nagaland benefited, the target for 2025-26; 
(b) the role of SECI in Nagaland’s renewable energy, the solar and hybrid projects initiated by SECI in Nagaland;
(c) the impact of NER incentives on Nagaland, the manner in which these incentives have benefited Nagaland’s projects;
(d) the impact of small hydro projects in North East States, the number of operational projects in Nagaland; and 
(e) the steps taken to promote green hydrogen in North East and the projects planned for Nagaland under the National Green Hydrogen Mission?

(a) the manner in which the Ministry is combating vector-borne diseases in Nagaland, what is the impact of National Vector Borne Disease Control Programme (NVBDCP) in Northeast States;
(b) whether the Ministry is considering the inclusion of a State-wide vaccination protocol to address the growing public health concern; 
(c) if so, the steps being taken to ensure timely implementation and coverage in the most effected regions; and
(d) the measures taken to address antimicrobial resistance in Northeast States, and the details of surveillance systems active in hospitals of Nagaland?

(a) the list of all schemes of the Central Government and programs currently being implemented in the State of Nagaland over the last years, including the number of beneficiaries under it;
(b) whether any initiatives undertaken to spread awareness among SC-ST entrepreneurs, if so, the details thereof;
(c) the achievement made due to implementation of the Public Procurement Policy for MSMEs and share of SC/ST and women-led MSEs over the last five years; and
(d) whether Government is considering new schemes, digital tools, handholding support to further enhance SC/ST and women-led MSEs in Government procurement?

(a) measures Government is taking to enhance MSME's access to credit in Nagaland, given the State's economic reliance on these enterprises, specific schemes that are in place to address this;
(b) manner in which Government is facilitating MSME's access to global markets from Nagaland;
(c) existing the export potential for MSMEs of Nagaland and trade facilitation programs in place; and
(d) manner in which the RAMP scheme is benefiting MSMEs in Nagaland, the RAMP scheme aims to enhance MSME performance, specific outcomes that have been achieved in Nagaland?

(a) the number of Anganwadi Centres (AWCs) approved to be transformed into Saksham Anganwadis in the country;
(b) the number of Anganwadi upgraded as of February, 2025 in the country; and
(c) the areas that are being focussed upon in the upgradation of Anganwadis in the country?

(a) whether Government plans to implement a structured and time-bound compensation framework for communities affected by human-elephant conflicts in Nagaland;
(b) the steps being taken to integrate bamboo cultivation into the Nagaland Forest Management Project (NFMP) as recommended by the Union Minister during his visit; and
(c) whether there are any plans to expand externally aided projects such as the Forest and Biodiversity Management in the Himalaya (KFW Project) and the NFMP to other regions facing similar environmental challenges?

(a) the measures being implemented by Government to harness the hydropower potential of the North Eastern Region;
(b) manner in which these initiatives aim to address the challenges associated with hydropower development in the region; and
(c) the financial assistance provided thereof?

(a) the manner in which the Indie haat initiative aligns with the objectives of Aatmanirbhar Bharat and Vocal for Local campaigns; 
(b) the role of Indie haat in promoting the export of Indian handicrafts and handloom products, particularly, the traditional crafts of Jharkhand; 
(c) the strategies Government is adopting to expand Indie Haat to reach a greater number of audiences domestically and internationally; and
(d) the steps being taken by Government to provide support to artisans and handloom enterprises of Jharkhand in terms of digitisation, branding and making exportable products?

(a) the details of the Central Government schemes currently available for handloom weavers in Nagaland;
(b) the number of artisans and weavers in Nagaland who have benefitted from these schemes in the last three years, district-wise;
(c) whether Government has conducted any impact assessment of these schemes in the State, and if so, the key findings; and
(d) whether Government has any plans to introduce new schemes or enhance existing ones to further support the handloom sector in Nagaland, and if so, the details thereof?

(a) the measures taken by Government to enhance agricultural productivity while ensuring sustainability in rural and marginalized communities;
(b) the steps taken by Government to integrate climate resilience into rural development policies; and
(c) the measures being taken to ensure that the benefits of rural development initiatives reach the most vulnerable sections of society, including women, small-scale farmers, and indigenous communities?

(a) the specific initiatives that have been introduced to facilitate the export of Self-Help Group (SHG) products;
(b) whether Government signed any Memorandum of Understanding (MoUs) with international buyers or trade bodies to promote Indian handicrafts in global markets;
(c) if so, the details thereof; and
(d) whether there are any collaborations with private sector companies or online platforms to ensure year-round marketing opportunities for SHG products beyond the Saras Aajeevika Mela; and
(e) if so, the details thereof?

(a) whether Government is implementing a programme 'Harnessing Yuva Shakti for Viksit Bharat'; 
(b) the measures taken to extend the reach of NSS and NYKS under the said programme to more and more students and youth, in the deprived areas including Maharashtra; 
(c) the manner in which the Youth Connect programme would address the aspirations and challenges of youth in rural and remote areas across the country, including Maharashtra; and
(d) the manner in which Government plans to integrate values like critical thinking and civic engagement in the curriculum of educational institutions as part of the Youth Connect programme?

(a) the mechanisms which are in place to ensure timely execution and quality control of the projects under PM-DevINE;
(b) the steps being taken to address administrative and logistical bottlenecks in States like Manipur and Meghalaya;
(c) the measures being taken to ensure that infrastructure projects under PM-DevINE incorporate sustainable and eco-friendly practices; and
(d) the manner in which the implementation of PM-DevINE projects contributed to employment generation and economic development in the North Eastern Region?

(a) the steps taken to ensure a balanced startup ecosystem across all the North Eastern States;
(b) the measures being taken to ensure that startups in the North Eastern Region have adequate access to funding including Venture Capital, Angel investments and debt facilities; and
(c) the specific schemes or incentives in place to encourage women and tribal entrepreneurs in the Startup ecosystem of the North Eastern region?

(a) the steps taken by Government to promote traditional handloom and handicraft products from Nagaland in both domestic and international markets;
(b) the financial support or subsidies available for artisans and weavers in Nagaland under the Ministry’s various schemes; and 
(c) whether Government has considered launching special initiatives to support the development of Naga weaving traditions, such as those associated with the traditional shawls, garments, and crafts unique to Nagaland?

(a) the schemes being implemented for the development of handloom sector;
(b) the benefits being provided to weavers/workers under the schemes; and
(c) the steps taken by Government to support and ensure welfare of weavers?

(a) the total number of Eklavya Model Residential Schools (EMRS) in Nagaland;
(b) the total number of non-functional EMRS and reasons thereof; 
(c) the fund allocated for the construction and operationalization of EMRS in Nagaland; and
(d) the percentage of the allocated funds utilized and the details thereof?

(a) specific data regarding the progress and impact of the Regional Connectivity Scheme (RCS) - UDAN since its inception;
(b) the number of routes and airports that have been operationalized under the UDAN scheme as of now;
(c) the total number of passengers benefited from this scheme till date; and
(d) the details on the financial allocation and utilization for airport development under UDAN scheme?

(a) the percentage of funds allocated to Nagaland and utilisation thereof under DoNER schemes in the last three years;
(b) the manner in which these funds have been distributed across sectors in Nagaland; and
(c) the primary reasons for underutilization, if any, and the measures being taken to address them?
